WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.749
This is the Daily Karma. Today’s practice is shinrin yoku: among the trees. Find a supported position. Let your eyes close, or rest gently on the painting.

2
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.520
Feel the surface beneath you. Unclench your jaw. Let your shoulders settle. For these five minutes, there is nowhere else you need to be.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.613
Feel the quiet rhythm of breathing. When the mind moves ahead, come back to one simple inhale and one unhurried exhale.

4
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:35.889
Shinrin yoku is not a walk with a destination. It is letting the senses take in a place without turning any of it into a task. Nothing is covered or achieved.

5
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:02.331
Standing among tall trees with the light coming down in pieces. Bark, damp earth, movement somewhere in the branches. You are not studying it; you are in it.

6
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:29.660
Notice what your body is doing with these words. Soften around the eyes, the hands, and the belly. Keep only the effort needed to stay present.

7
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:57.567
Let one sense lead for a moment. Sound, probably, with the eyes closed. Let it arrive without naming it or deciding what it means.

8
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:25.985
I will leave some quiet here. You do not need to empty the mind. Notice what appears, release the story, and return to breathing.

9
00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.845
Still here. Still breathing. Nothing special needs to happen. This quiet awareness is already a useful way of meeting your life.

10
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:27.449
Give five minutes to your senses today. Outside if you can, a window if you cannot. Look without photographing, listen without naming.

11
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:52.799
Notice the sounds around you. Invite movement back into your hands and feet. Open your eyes softly. Thank you for meeting this day with Karma.
